From: afni-win
Subject: [PATCH] 3dttest++: start -Clustsim jobs without fork on Windows

Why the compat layer cannot handle this: start_job() calls fork(); the
child only runs system(cmd) and exits, the parent records the pid and later
waits with wait(). fork() must return twice, which no library can provide
on Windows, so the call site has to change. Under _WIN32 the patch starts
"sh -c cmd" asynchronously with afni_compat_spawn_shell() (same shell as
system(), child registered for wait()/waitpid()), which is what the forked
child did. The error path (kill() of earlier jobs) and wait_for_jobs() are
unchanged; the layer implements kill(SIGTERM) and wait().

diff --git a/src/3dttest++.c b/src/3dttest++.c
index 8f940f1..38c6615 100644
--- a/src/3dttest++.c
+++ b/src/3dttest++.c
@@ -2374,7 +2374,14 @@ void start_job( char *cmd )   /* 10 Feb 2016 */
    if( cmd == NULL || *cmd == '\0' ) return ;
 
    errno = 0 ;
+#ifdef _WIN32
+   /* afni-win: no fork() on Windows; the child below would only run
+      system(cmd), so start "sh -c cmd" directly without waiting for it */
+   errno = afni_compat_spawn_shell( &newid , cmd ) ;
+   if( errno != 0 ) newid = (pid_t)-1 ;
+#else
    newid = fork() ;
+#endif
 
    if( newid == (pid_t)-1 ){  /*--- fork failed -- should never happen ---*/
 
